  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "style": "Title",
      "text": "Can a draft assistant preserve the limits in a workshop information sheet?"
    },
    {
      "style": "Subtitle",
      "text": "Applied AI Workflow Case · D11-A · Revision 1 · 3 October 2026"
    },
    {
      "style": "Caption",
      "text": "Workflow route · Evidence register · Next step"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Fictional demonstration. Northbank Workshop, the people, documents, questions, assistant responses and…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "01 / Decision and audience"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Decision: retain a human-written publication step and prepare a controlled evaluation before…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "This case is for the workshop coordinator and a teaching colleague reviewing a possible drafting aid.…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The useful output is a review queue: question, candidate answer, source line, uncertainty and human…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "02 / Inputs and boundaries"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The fictional source is a versioned, public-facing information sheet, NB-SHEET-01 v1. Four lines are…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Only these four lines and eight invented questions enter the proposed drafting step. There are no…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Model, provider, release, temperature, retention configuration and deployment environment are not…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "03 / Before and proposed after"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Before: Mina reads a question, opens the current information sheet, writes an answer with its limits,…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Proposed after: Mina first checks the input and source version at H1. An assistant prepares an answer…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "This table is the complete textual equivalent of the schematic. The diagram shows the same routes,…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading2",
      "text": "Workflow blueprint"
    },
    {
      "style": "Caption",
      "text": "Proposed workflow — no execution measured."
    },
    {
      "style": "Caption",
      "text": "Arrows name permitted next steps. They do not encode speed, volume or successful completion. The…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "04 / Drafting instruction and comparison rule"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The proposed instruction is: “Use only NB-SHEET-01 v1. Answer the supplied question in at most two…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "This instruction is an editable evaluation input, not evidence that a model would comply. The responses…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The unit is one submitted question. There are eight questions in the fixture, including questions with…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "05 / Complete authored trace register"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "06 / Failure, counterevidence and remaining uncertainty"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Q03 demonstrates a condition being lost while the main date remains plausible. Q04 demonstrates an…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Q01 and Q02 are counterexamples to the idea that every drafted answer requires rewriting: these…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "The case contains no observation of model behavior, elapsed time, cost, accessibility experience,…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "07 / Evidence register"
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading1",
      "text": "08 / Next step and publication boundary"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Mina’s fictional next step is to design a bounded evaluation with a colleague. Before running it, they…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "They would record all attempted questions, exclusions and reasons, unsupported claims, omitted…"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "text": "Until that evidence exists, the publication-ready conclusion is limited: this fictional trace…"
    }
